4f2d-b6e4-7b23b6600357"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0df839ec8d561e24fcfc2e943599204d52bfc0b3b5c1a13450e6634d23cd8fab","event_uuid":"db33a7a4-2d29-441e-92e2-1aa8b4b2be2a","position":{"commit_sha":"e96d0e615b9682ca198f606c72ea0178c8f039e8","position":"1787621971534368001-db33a7a4-2d29-441e-92e2-1aa8b4b2be2a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed via Gerrit change 2204 (patchset 3): LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Per-client bearer PATs materialized on-box from SSM (token_env → mcp-static-tokens.json), gitignored + rsync-excluded; runbook documents operator-driven rotation.","timestamp":1787621971534368001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787594476500443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bcc6a6d2-3809-4a45-9421-bfbea1c1a7aa","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"},{"link_uuid":"44cf19fd-262c-4432-8856-48ff12b85033","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"65ac-c8ef-b5b8-4d7a"},{"link_uuid":"d8407b6c-4ac3-4b71-9e93-37c5d30abf66","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5fba-b56f-450d-4a09"},{"link_uuid":"1a644611-7827-4f74-a70f-662d45badaf0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4011-d0e5-41e1-4e60"}],"description":"Provision the per-client bearer PATs the `static` verifier authenticates (ADR\ndeft-evolutive-mosasaur) and the repo-root local-only client-credential config the epic asks for,\ntreated like every other box secret: SSM-sourced, materialized on-box, gitignored, never committed.\nSingle concern: the credential material + its safe delivery — client-side config wiring is olm.\n\n## Approach + rationale (SSM-materialize, NOT rsync — gotcha f600)\nThe `.env` on the box is rsync-EXCLUDED, so a rotated SSM secret never reaches the box via source\nsync. The bearer PATs must therefore be materialized on the box from SSM at deploy time, exactly\nlike the existing `opcert-guard.map.conf` materialization pattern (a separate SSM-sourced file that\nnginx/the app reads), NOT baked into the rsync'd tree. A pure value-rotation (no git change) does\nNOT advance `main`, so autodeploy no-ops on it — rotation is operator-driven (re-materialize +\nreload), which the runbook must state. Because the `static` verifier loads its token set ONCE at\n`__init__` (`StaticBearerVerifier.__init__` → `_load_static_tokens`; no per-request re-read),\n\"reload\" here means RECONSTRUCTING the verifier — i.e. restarting/replacing the `rebar-mcp`\nprocess/container (the ADR 0104 blue-green swap) — NOT merely rewriting the tokens file; an\noperator who only re-materializes the file sees NO effect. The runbook states this explicitly.\n- Terraform SSM params for the per-client PATs (one per client: copilot/codex/claude) under the\n  existing `/rebar/prod/` prefix; `fetch-secrets.sh` wiring to materialize them on the box.\n- The `static` verifier's accepted-token set is sourced from those materialized secrets. Transform\n  (named so the slice is unambiguous): `fetch-secrets.sh` materializes each per-client PAT from SSM\n  into the on-box container env source (`.env`, 0600, rsync-excluded) as\n  `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_{COPILOT,CODEX,CLAUDE}`, and emits the tokens JSON the verifier reads\n  (`infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json`, `mcp.auth_static_tokens_file`) whose records reference\n  those env vars via **`token_env`** — NEVER a plaintext `token` and NEVER the raw PAT inside the\n  tokens file (ADR 0050 §4 / ADR 0104: the server holds only SHA-256 digests, supplied via env-var\n  NAMES, never literals; `_parse_static_record` rejects a plaintext `token`). The tokens file is\n  ALWAYS created even when a slot is blank (bug beb1: a missing bind-mount source becomes a\n  directory).\n- A **repo-root local-only** client-credential config TEMPLATE (committed placeholder-only) —\n  `mcp-clients.local.example.json` — that renders to a real gitignored file `mcp-clients.local.json`\n  (`.gitignore` pattern `/mcp-clients.local.json`), so an operator wiring a client has a documented\n  shape but no secret is ever committed.\n- Enumerated gitignore/rsync edits so the materialized artifacts are BOTH gitignored and\n  rsync-protected (mirroring the `.env` precedent): add `infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` (and\n  its `.*` temp variants) plus `/mcp-clients.local.json` to the root `.gitignore`, and add\n  `--exclude 'infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json'` to `autodeploy.sh` RSYNC_EXCLUDES (~line 163),\n  so a value-only re-materialize is never clobbered by `rsync --delete`.\n- Blank-slot behavior: `fetch-secrets.sh` OMITS the `token_env` record for any client whose\n  `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_*` slot is unset/empty (so `_parse_static_record` never sees an empty `token_env`\n  and cannot fail the whole verifier). The file is still ALWAYS created (beb1); when ALL slots are\n  blank it is `{\"tokens\": []}`, and the `static` verifier then fails-closed at startup\n  (`_load_static_tokens` raises \"defines no tokens\") — the intended state until an operator\n  populates at least one PAT.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Tier: **real file/CLI + a committed-secret guard test** (test-design §3 CLI + §6 contrast). Oracles:\n  - The gitignored real credential path `mcp-clients.local.json` is matched by `.gitignore` and a\n    guard test asserts `git check-ignore` returns it AND that no file in the tree contains a real PAT\n    pattern (the negative control: the committed template `mcp-clients.local.example.json` with a\n    placeholder passes; a planted real-looking secret fails). Proof:\n    `pytest tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py -k guard`.\n  - `fetch-secrets.sh` materializes the per-client PATs from SSM: the raw value lands ONLY in the\n    0600 rsync-excluded env source (`.env` as `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_*`), and the tokens JSON the `static`\n    verifier reads (`mcp-static-tokens.json`) references it via `token_env` (never a plaintext\n    `token`, never the raw value in the tokens file). Oracle: with a stubbed SSM/aws sink feeding a\n    known value → the materialized env source contains the value AND the tokens file loads via the\n    real `_load_static_tokens`/`_parse_static_record` path (token_env records); both files are\n    gitignored (NOT under the rsync'd tree), and the tokens file is created even when a slot is\n    blank (beb1). Proof: `pytest tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py -k materialize`.\n  - Config-effect contrast (§6): the `static` verifier (`StaticBearerVerifier` over the materialized\n    tokens file with the per-client env var set) accepts a request bearing a materialized PAT and\n    rejects an unknown token (401) through the real `_load_static_tokens` read path. Proof:\n    `pytest tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py -k verifier`.\n- [x] The runbook documents operator-driven rotation (re-materialize + restart/replace the\n  `rebar-mcp` process/container so the verifier re-reads the tokens file; autodeploy no-ops on a\n  value-only rotation). Proof: checked via `pytest tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py -k runbook`\n  asserting `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md` documents the re-materialize + reload (restart)\n  rotation and that a file-only rewrite has no effect on a running verifier.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py` — the guard, materialization, verifier-contrast,\n  and runbook oracles above (RED-first; the ACs are the oracle).\n- `make lint && make typecheck` — gate the new Python test module + touched sources.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive (new SSM params + materialization). Rollback = remove the params + materialization step;\nno existing secret path changes. Never commits a secret (enforced by the guard test above).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR fixes the auth mode = static bearer). Blocks:\nunmythical-uninspired-olm (client configs need the PAT values).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/ssm.tf","reason":"Declare per-client MCP bearer PAT SSM SecureString params (copilot/codex/claude) under /rebar/prod/."},{"path":"infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","reason":"Materialize per-client PATs into .env and emit the static-tokens JSON (token_env records) the verifier reads."},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Exclude the materialized mcp-static-tokens.json from rsync --delete so a value-only re-materialize is not clobbered."},{"path":".gitignore","reason":"Ignore the materialized tokens file and the real local client-credential config so no secret is committed."},{"path":"mcp-clients.local.example.json","reason":"Committed placeholder-only client-credential config template that renders to the gitignored real file."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md","reason":"Operator-driven rotation runbook (re-materialize + restart rebar-mcp; autodeploy no-ops on value-only rotation)."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py","reason":"Guard, materialization, verifier-contrast, and runbook oracle tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"],["relates_to","4011-d0e5-41e1-4e60"],["relates_to","5fba-b56f-450d-4a09"],["relates_to","65ac-c8ef-b5b8-4d7a"]],"n